 ## Background
-The concept of Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF) was introduced by Mildenhall et al. in 2020 [G]. This work established the paradigm of using MLPs to represent continuous 3D scenes for novel view synthesis [G]. Subsequent works, such as [PixelNeRF](7471-pixelnerf.md), extended this to sparse-view settings by incorporating CNN-extracted features. The [Attenuation Field](9639-attenuation-field.md) approach adapts this implicit representation for medical X-ray imaging, replacing the radiance model with the Beer–Lambert law.
